# WORKFLOW — Write Map, Tempo, Swarm, Probing & Lore

File: openOODA/WORKFLOW.oot
Write map, tempo, swarm, and bug lore. Read section 0 before any edit.
This board maps where to write and how to run turns. Section 0 is the product write map. Section 1 is OODA tempo. Section 2 is the Multi-Agent Concurrent Swarm Protocol. Section 3 is adversarial validation. Section 4 is token economy. Section 5 is bug lore.

## 0. Product Write Map — What Changes Where

Three public places. That is the whole public system.
  Door     ../openOODA.github.io/index.html     https://openooda.org/
  Guide    ../openOODA.github.io/guide/*.oot    https://openooda.org/guide/
  Store    ../registry/                         https://registry.openooda.org/
Do not add research to nav. Files under ../openOODA.github.io/research/ stay so old URLs do not 404.

### 0.1 If you ship this, write here

  Package manager / ooda add / ingest / launch
    ../ooda/cli/cmd_pm*.oo  ../ooda/cli/pm_*.oo  ../ooda/cli/main.oo
    Proof: ../ooda/cli/*_proof.oo and ../qa/pm_*_spine.oo
    ../ooda/pm/ is a stub. Do not grow it.
    Coordinate shared files with active swarm peers under the Concurrent Swarm Protocol.

  Compiler / language
    ../ooda/oodac/*.oo and named ../ooda/scripts/*_smoke.oo
    Official rebuild: ../ooda/bootstrap/oodac_pure_build
    Never copy ./bin/ooda onto ./oodac/oodac.

  Runtime C
    ../ooda/runtime/ — RT role only.
  Standard library
    ../ooda/std/  Ships with compiler. Prove emit+gcc+run before calling a folder product.

  Safety that is true today
    ../openOODA.github.io/guide/Safety.oot
    New guide page: add the .oot and add its name to guide/index.html PAGES.

  How-to, options, limits
    ../openOODA.github.io/guide/{Home,Use,Options,Limits}.oot

  Design / moonshot / not shipped
    ../openOODA.github.io/research/*.oot stay on disk. Do not link from door or guide.
    Do not add research nav item. Do not paste moonshots into guide as product.

  RFC / design proposal
    openOODA/rfcs/NNNN-name.oot — copy rfcs/0000-template.oot, Status Draft→Active→Accepted→Implemented. Verify Security & Testing criteria per template.

  Public install
    From a checkout:
      OODA_FS_WRITEDIR=$HOME OODA_CHECKOUT=$PWD ooda install
    Payload is host bash script (openOODA.github.io/install.sh). Run `curl -fsSL https://openooda.org/install.sh | bash`.
    Real installer: ../ooda/install/install.oo
    First machine still needs tree, gcc, and seed rebuild. Old `/install` redirects to `/install.sh`.

  Public package
    ../registry/<name>/manifest and payload .oo
    Rewrite registry/index (pipe rows). Copy those bytes to catalog.
    Sign: minisign -S -s ~/.ooda-keys/registry.secret.key -m index -x index.minisig
    Update human index.html. CLI verifies catalog with ../ooda/cli/registry.pub
    Never commit secret. Browsers hit /. CLI GETs /catalog.

  Process, pin, proved inventory
    The twelve boards in this folder. SHIPPED is generated via `scripts/generate_shipped.oo` only after proof. Do not hand-edit.

  Hostile product proofs
    ../qa/pm_*_spine.oo or ../ooda/scripts/*_smoke.oo

### 0.2 Do not write

  ../wiki/ and ../docs/    local clones removed. GitHub wiki and docs repos archived.
  leftover GitHub repos named research or install
                           those steal https://openooda.org/research and /install.sh.
  Guide lives at /guide/. /research/ is an archive URL, not a nav item.
  ~/.ooda-keys/            secrets stay off git.

### 0.3 Site rules and publish

  One-bit Macintosh: white or black, monospace, title-bar wordmark.
  Theme toggle bottom-right. Version pin in header links to GitHub release notes. Cookie ooda-theme on .openooda.org.
  Public links stay on openooda.org. Link github.com only to visit GitHub.
  Site and registry: commit and push. GitHub Pages serves them.
  Product: commit in ../ooda/. Do not push secrets.

## 1. OODA Loop Tempo & Rotation Lifecycle

The OODA rotation guarantees continuous progress, verifiable quality, and clean git history on every turn.

1. Observe
  - Read section 0 so the edit lands in the right tree.
  - Read active handoffs and release pin (`v2.5.3`) in `ROADMAP.oot`.
  - Skim Section 5 (Bug Lore) below to avoid past failure modes.
  - Inspect repository health: line counts (<= 256 lines), cruft, failed tests.
  - Identify I/O, subprocess execution, FFI, or capability attack surfaces.
  - Review swarm requirements: coordinate live disk state with active peers.
  - Define the single best next product step before taking action.

2. Decide (At Most 5 Items)
  Prioritize tasks in strict order:
    1. Broken tests and failed product rail checks.
    2. Honesty and security vulnerabilities that permit invalid execution.
    3. Next scheduled backlog item directly serving DESIGN.
    4. DESIGN architectural gap (document in backlog first, then build).
    5. Code hygiene and refactoring (if blocking or cheap).
  Decide Swarm Topology:
    - Solo: single agent owning a focused task; document reason.
    - Concurrent Swarm: multi-agent collaboration with live git synchronization.
    - Anti-Pattern: Never assign multiple agents to debug the same stuck issue.

3. Act
  - Write comments, boards, and user text in ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English.
  - Implement changes strictly on the real product path.
  - Execute under the Swarm Plan determined during Decide.
  - Maintain the 256-line ceiling per file; split modules at clean seams.
  - Deliver executable tests with behavioral assertions alongside code changes.
  - Zero secrets in codebase, configs, or logs.

4. Lock
  - Run verification: line counts, dead code, secrets, temporary artifacts.
  - Execute project rails and pure `.oo` test suites.
  - Regenerate SHIPPED via `scripts/generate_shipped.oo` and verify freshness.
  - Independently verify all assertions; never mark a task done without direct proof.
  - Ensure no orphaned background subagents or dangling processes remain.
  - If hygiene fails, do not proceed to Ship: repair violations immediately.

5. Ship
  - Create atomic commits with descriptive messages.
  - Write the handoff in ASD-STE100: what changed, why it matters, what is not done.
  - Record execution topology: solo rationale or swarm peer role breakdown.

Session Adapter Template:
  ROOT: /path/to/project
  Product binaries / build command: ./bin/ooda or oodac_pure_build
  Backlog / Handoff / Release Pin: ROADMAP.oot (v2.5.3)
  Rails: ./bin/ooda check_all / scripts/enforcer.oo
  SWARM plan: solo (<reason>) OR swarm (<agent>: <owned files>)

## 2. Multi-Agent Concurrent Swarm Protocol (Pillar 6)

All autonomous agents operating in this repository must follow the 4-part Concurrent Swarm Protocol:

1. Continuous Live Git & Disk Awareness:
   - Always re-read target files from disk and pull latest git state before editing.
   - Never rely on cached file contents across turns or tool executions.
   - Detect upstream merges and synchronize shared state dynamically.

2. Cooperative Non-Clobbering Integration:
   - Coordinate task assignments across the swarm to prevent overlapping file mutations.
   - Make atomic, granular commits that preserve peer modifications.
   - Use clean modular boundaries and interfaces to allow parallel development.

3. Version-Tagged Checkpoints & Structured Handoffs:
   - Document all changes in 5-component handoff reports (Observation, Logic Chain, Caveats, Conclusion, Verification Method).
   - Record exact file paths, line numbers, tool commands, and test outputs.
   - Tag milestones with Generational SemVer (`v<Floor>.<Thrust>.<Patch>`, pinned to `v2.5.3`).
   - Obey Power Law 80/20 Weighted Floor Rule: Floor increments only when the 20% core substrate shifts.

4. The 4-Step Verification Gate:
   - Step 1: Syntax and type check (`./bin/ooda check <file.oo>`).
   - Step 2: Sequential double-run binary execution proof (`./bin/ooda run <test.oo>`).
   - Step 3: Adversarial testing with malformed/forged inputs (must fail closed).
   - Step 4: Master governance lint check (`enforcer.oo` with 0 violations).

## 3. Adversarial Validation & Negative Trust (Pillar 3)

Core Law: Green tests are hypotheses, not proofs. Adversarial validation actively attacks the assumptions behind code, documentation, and compiler output.

Verification Roles:
  - Orchestrator: Schedules test suites, coordinates runs, and compiles audit reports.
  - Worker: Injects hostile faults, mutation tests, and implements fixes on product binaries.
  - Independent Verifier: Re-executes claims in fresh environments; falsifies claims with hostile probes.

The Sequential Double-Run Law:
  Execute `./bin/ooda run <test.oo>` twice sequentially in clean processes. Both runs must pass identically to prove deterministic memory safety and zero state leakage.

Hostile Probing Vectors:
  1. Boundary & Invariants:
     - Missing capability tokens fail closed with explicit errors.
     - Forged, zero, or un-granted capability tokens are rejected at runtime.
     - Corrupted inputs, inverted values, and malformed structures trigger safe exits.
  2. Robustness & Resources:
     - Resource limits: file descriptor exhaustion, tight heap budgets without crash.
     - Read-only directories: non-zero exit on write attempts without ambient escape.
     - Concurrent fuzzing: no deadlocks, race conditions, or memory corruption.
     - Hang budget: 5 to 10 seconds maximum per test; hangs fail closed as CRIT.
  3. Lifecycle & Cleanup:
     - All file and socket descriptors closed across error and success paths.
     - Child processes cleanly reaped without zombie processes.
     - Temporary files deleted in teardown routines.
  4. Anti-Synthetic Verification:
     - Test distributed binaries directly (never mock underlying subsystems).
     - Validate unmasked return codes directly (no masking behind shell pipes).

Finding Severity Hierarchy:
  - CRIT: Security bypass, capability forgery, or unauthorized success on product path.
  - HIGH: Fail-open behavior, execution hang, silent data corruption, or dropped errors.
  - MED:  Handle/memory leaks, incomplete capability seals, or hygiene debt.
  - LOW:  Documentation drift, comment mismatch, or minor metric discrepancies.

## 4. Token Economy & Sparing Ingress

Context is finite. Verbose prose steals reasoning budget.
Use `./bin/ooda outline <file.oo>` and `./bin/ooda reflect <file.oo> [sym]` to inspect code cheaply.
Canonical files mark `canonical: yes`. Short-form files mark `canonical: no`.
Use canonical for design and review; use short-form for large multi-file migrations.
Never load raw emit dumps (`all*.c`), full ROADMAP.oot, or raw gcc error walls into context.

## 5. Hard-Won System Lore & Bug Lessons

1. AST Injection:
   C macro injection in comma expressions cannot parse un-braced constructs. Always inject `((void)0)` instead of `do {} while(0)`. (Learned 2026-08-11)
2. Decoy Memory Offsets:
   The compiler shuffles `__oo_meta_decoy_*` struct layouts at runtime. Tests must never assume fixed static struct offsets. (Learned 2026-08-12)
3. HITL & Process Policy:
   HITL tests and configs must invoke `oo_process_policy_getenv` to respect security policy rather than raw host `getenv`. (Learned 2026-08-11)
4. Capability Gating:
   All new standard library, crypto, or network primitives must fail closed with `process_exit(1)` until formal audit verification lands. (Learned 2026-08-12)
5. AST Imports:
   Import tokens must be represented as distinct `IMPORT` AST nodes to ensure file boundaries remain concrete and `item_idx` increments accurately. (Learned 2026-08-12)
6. Script Conventions:
   All smoke tests and utility scripts are pure `.oo` files under `ooda/scripts/*_smoke.oo`. Never create `.oos`, `.sh`, or `.py` files. (Learned 2026-08-13)
7. FFI Handle Locks:
   Host dynamic library operations (`oo_dlopen`) require `&UnsafeFFICap` and must lock the FFI mutex to prevent nested invocation races. (Learned 2026-08-14)
8. Product CLI String Traps:
   Do not write `str_index_of(...) == 0` or `!= 0`. Do not write `String != String`. Do not mutate a slurp String named `lock`, `lk`, or `src`. `"\r"` is not CR. Writes go through `write_file` under `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR`.
9. Binary Identity Law:
   Never copy CLI onto compiler. Identity is `grep -a` only. No Cargo. No ELF transmutation.

